  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What State Is in React",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==State== is any value that changes over time __and__ must trigger a **re-render** when it changes. No re-render needed? Not state.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "state",
                "sub": "the input"
              },
              {
                "text": "f( )",
                "sub": "your component",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "UI tree",
                "sub": "the output"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "React is a __pure function of state__: same state in, same tree out. Every render recomputes from scratch.",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. State vs Its Neighbours",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Holder",
            "Survives render?",
            "Re-renders?",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`let x = 0`",
              "**no**, resets",
              "no",
              "scratch math"
            ],
            [
              "`useRef()`",
              "yes",
              "**no**",
              "timer id, DOM node"
            ],
            [
              "`useState()`",
              "yes",
              "**yes**",
              "visible values"
            ],
            [
              "props",
              "yes (from parent)",
              "yes, parent-driven",
              "read-only input"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Props vs State",
          "items": [
            "Props flow __down__; child treats them as ==read-only==",
            "State is owned + set by the component that declares it",
            "Child wants change? Parent passes a setter down"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: isOpen vs timestamp",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [isOpen, setOpen] =",
            "  useState(false);   // paints",
            "const openedAt = useRef(0);",
            "",
            "function open() {",
            "  openedAt.current = Date.now();",
            "  setOpen(true);",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "log-only value goes in a ref"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`isOpen` drives the modal, so it is **state**. `openedAtTimestamp` is only read by a logger, so a {purple:ref} is right — writing it must not repaint.",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Four Kinds of App Data",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Kind",
            "Example",
            "Right tool"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Local UI",
              "modal open, tab",
              "useState"
            ],
            [
              "Form",
              "draft fields, errors",
              "useState / reducer"
            ],
            [
              "URL",
              "`?page=2`, route id",
              "router, not state"
            ],
            [
              "Server cache",
              "fetched user list",
              "query cache"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "UI = f(state)"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "useState: The Basic Hook",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Server ≠ client state",
          "text": "API data is a ==cache with staleness==, not a value a reducer owns. It can go stale behind your back; local state never does."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Storing `fullName` in a **second** useState — derive it in render",
            "Duplicating one value in two places — it __will drift__",
            "Using state for a mouse position only a `<canvas>` reads",
            "Keeping a plain `let` and wondering why nothing repaints"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// derived, not state",
            "const full = first + ' ' + last;"
          ],
          "note": "free on every render, never stale"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Single source of truth",
          "text": "Each fact lives in exactly **one** place. Everything else is computed from it. Next: `useState` itself — page 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Signature",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [value, setValue] =",
            "  useState(initialValue)",
            "// tuple, read BY POSITION",
            "const [n, setN] = useState(0)"
          ],
          "note": "names are yours, order is not"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Returns a __2-slot tuple__: current value, then setter",
            "Destructured by ==position==, never by name",
            "`initialValue` used on **first** render of that instance only",
            "Later renders pass it and React __ignores__ it"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Lazy Initializer",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// BAD: runs every render",
            "useState(expensiveParse(json))",
            "// GOOD: runs once",
            "useState(() => expensiveParse(json))"
          ],
          "note": "pass the function, do not call it"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Why the bad one hurts",
          "text": "`expensiveParse(json)` is an ==argument==, so JS evaluates it every render. React just **discards** the result after render 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Updater Forms",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Reads",
            "3 calls give"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`setC(count + 1)`",
              "closure snapshot",
              "**+1**"
            ],
            [
              "`setC(c => c + 1)`",
              "latest queued",
              "**+3**"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Why +1 not +3",
          "items": [
            "`count` is a __const__ frozen in this render",
            "All three read `0`, all queue `1`",
            "Updater gets the ==queued== value, not the snapshot",
            "Rule: new value depends on old {red:use the function}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useEffect` reset renders **twice** and can loop",
            "A changed ==key== throws the old state away for free",
            "Only for state that must die with the prop"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "Signature to update rules"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Immutability and the Render Phase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Immutability Contract",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "items.push(x)",
            "setItems(items) // NOTHING",
            "setItems([...items, x]) // ok"
          ],
          "note": "same reference = React bails out"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Change",
            "Pattern"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "add",
              "`[...items, x]`"
            ],
            [
              "remove",
              "`items.filter(i=>i.id!==id)`"
            ],
            [
              "field",
              "`{...obj, key: v}`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Bailout==: new value `Object.is`-equal to old {orange:may skip re-render}",
            "Mutation keeps the reference, so it __always__ bails",
            "Setter identity is ==stable forever== {green:omit from deps}"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Resetting on Prop Change",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// NOT an effect + setter",
            "<Form key={userId} user={u} />"
          ],
          "note": "new key = fresh instance, fresh state"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Page in one line",
          "text": "Init once, update with a __function__ when the new value depends on the old, and always hand React a **new reference**."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Render Is a Phase",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "==Render== is React calling your component function to produce a __description__ of UI. No pixels move yet. Painting happens later, in commit.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "RENDER",
                "sub": "call fn",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "RECONCILE",
                "sub": "diff tree",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "COMMIT",
                "sub": "DOM mutations",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Update Queue",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Each `setState` call ==pushes an update== onto that hook's queue",
            "Queue is **drained** at the start of the next render",
            "Handler returns first, then React schedules one render",
            "Parent re-render re-renders __all children__ by default, props changed or not"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Batching",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Source",
            "React 17",
            "React 18+"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "onClick handler",
              "batched",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "`setTimeout`",
              "**no**",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "`.then()` promise",
              "**no**",
              "batched"
            ],
            [
              "native listener",
              "**no**",
              "batched"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "setA(1); setB(2); setC(3);",
            "// 3 updates = ONE re-render",
            "",
            "flushSync(() => setX(v));",
            "// forces sync render + commit",
            "const h = ref.current.offsetHeight;"
          ],
          "note": "flushSync only when you must read layout"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Why it logs the old value",
          "items": [
            "`count` is a **const** binding of __this__ render",
            "`onClick` closed over that binding forever",
            "New value only exists in the ==next== render's `count`",
            "Need it now? Compute `count + 1` yourself"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "Render, batch, commit"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Closures, Hook Order, and Dispatch",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Closure Snapshot",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "function Counter() {",
            "  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)",
            "  const onClick = () => {",
            "    setCount(count + 1)",
            "    console.log(count) // 0, NOT 1",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "count is const in this render"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Hooks Are a Linked List",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "On the fiber",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Each hook is a node; the fiber holds `memoizedState` head.",
                "icon": "react",
                "ink": "pink"
              },
              {
                "title": "Matched by order",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "Call #1 → node #1. React stores ==no names==, only position.",
                "ink": "pink"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No hooks inside `if` / `for` / `while`",
            "No hooks after an **early return**",
            "Only in components and `useXxx` custom hooks",
            "Skip one call and every later hook reads the __wrong__ node"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Pin this",
          "text": "setState is a request, not an assignment. You get a NEW render with a new count — you never mutate the old one."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Render = compute, reconcile = diff, commit = DOM",
            "One event handler = one re-render (18+ everywhere)",
            "Handler state = the snapshot of its own render",
            "Hook order is the identity — keep it fixed"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A hook that moves every update into one ==pure function==. You stop calling setters and start __dispatching actions__.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const [state, dispatch] =",
            "  useReducer(reducer, initArg, init?)",
            "// reducer: (state, action) => next"
          ],
          "note": "init is optional, lazy"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two facts you can lean on",
          "items": [
            "`init`: `useReducer(r, userId, createState)` runs once",
            "`dispatch` identity is ==stable forever==",
            "Safe in `useEffect` deps; never re-fires",
            "Pass deep through context — no `useMemo` needed"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "4 setters → 1 reducer",
          "text": "Four `useState` setters scatter cart rules into four handlers. One reducer is the **single edit surface** — every rule lives in one switch."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "Render, batch, commit"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "useReducer: State as Transitions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "function cart(state, action) {",
            "  switch (action.type) {",
            "    case 'add': return {...state,",
            "      items:[...state.items, action.payload]}",
            "    default: throw Error(action.type)",
            "  }",
            "}"
          ],
          "note": "pure: no fetch, no random"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rules of the reducer",
          "items": [
            "Pure: same input, same output, always",
            "No `Math.random()`, no `Date.now()`, no fetch",
            "Action shape: `{ type: 'added', payload }`",
            "`default: throw` catches typo'd action types"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: one cart, four actions",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Action",
            "Payload",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`add`",
              "item",
              "append to items"
            ],
            [
              "`remove`",
              "id",
              "filter out id"
            ],
            [
              "`setQty`",
              "{id, n}",
              "map, replace qty"
            ],
            [
              "`clear`",
              "—",
              "`{items: []}`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. When it beats useState",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Next state depends on previous in non-trivial ways",
            "Several fields must change ==together==, atomically",
            "Same update logic fires from many call sites",
            "Model {red:impossible states} out of existence"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "tables",
          "spec": {
            "tables": [
              {
                "title": "3 booleans = 8 states",
                "headers": [
                  "loading",
                  "error",
                  "data"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "true",
                    "true",
                    "yes ?!"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "5 of 8 are nonsense"
              },
              {
                "title": "1 union = 4 states",
                "headers": [
                  "status"
                ],
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "'idle'"
                  ],
                  [
                    "'loading' | 'error'"
                  ],
                  [
                    "'success'"
                  ]
                ],
                "caption": "all 4 are legal"
              }
            ],
            "arrow": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// no React, no render, no DOM",
            "expect(",
            "  cart({items:[]}, {type:'add',payload:x})",
            ").toEqual({items:[x]})"
          ],
          "note": "reducers unit-test as plain functions"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Two mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`state.items.push(x)` — mutation, same ref, __no re-render__. Return a new object",
            "Dispatch in a loop then reading `state` — you read the **old** render's snapshot",
            "Fix: fold the loop into one action, or read next state in the reducer"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Summary",
          "text": "useState scatters transitions; useReducer names them. One pure `(state, action)` function, a stable `dispatch`, and state changes become a ==testable, loggable list of transitions==."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Five setters: validation duplicated in `onChange` and `onSubmit`",
            "One reducer: `validate` runs on **every** `field_changed`, free",
            "Reducer tests: `reducer(state, {type:'submitted'})` — no render"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "green"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "One pure update function"
    },
