    {
      "page_title": "Lifting State to Its Owner",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Anti-patterns",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One `useReducer` holding ==unrelated slices== only to dodge many `useState` calls",
            "`useState({a,b,c})` then spreading on every update — you built a **worse** reducer",
            "Reaching for a reducer for a single boolean toggle — pure overhead",
            "Picking by identity stability — both are stable, __no advantage either way__"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule",
          "text": "Count the setters in your busiest handler. One or two, keep `useState`. Three, the transition is already **real** — give it a name and a reducer."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Lifting Up",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Two siblings need the same value: move it to their ==closest common ancestor== and pass it back down as props.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "Lift to Nearest Owner",
            "rows": [
              [
                "form"
              ],
              [
                "input",
                "preview"
              ]
            ],
            "nodes": {
              "form": {
                "text": "SearchForm",
                "shape": "box",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              "input": {
                "text": "<Input/>",
                "shape": "pill"
              },
              "preview": {
                "text": "<Results/>",
                "shape": "pill"
              }
            },
            "edges": [
              {
                "from": "form",
                "to": "input",
                "label": "value+onChange"
              },
              {
                "from": "form",
                "to": "preview",
                "label": "query"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Controlled vs Uncontrolled",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "Controlled",
            "Uncontrolled"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "value from",
              "parent state",
              "own DOM node"
            ],
            [
              "needs",
              "`value`+`onChange`",
              "`defaultValue`"
            ],
            [
              "read by",
              "render",
              "`ref.current.value`"
            ],
            [
              "parent sees",
              "every keystroke",
              "only on submit"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<input value={q}",
            "  onChange={e=>setQ(e.target.value)}/>",
            "",
            "<input defaultValue=\"hi\"",
            "  ref={inputRef}/>  // DOM owns it"
          ],
          "note": "never mix value with defaultValue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Colocation: Push It Down",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lifting is a cost — the whole subtree below re-renders",
            "Push state as far **DOWN** as it can go",
            "Smallest subtree that needs it is the right owner",
            "Modal's open flag lives in the modal's parent, not App"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Not a perf bug",
          "text": "Drilling is a ==readability== problem first, a **refactor-friction** problem second. Props are free to pass; renaming one across 4 files is what hurts."
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Where state should live"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Prop Drilling and Composition",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Prop Drilling",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Threading `user` through __components that never read it__, only to reach a deep consumer.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "chain",
          "spec": {
            "title": "user: 3 hops, 2 wasted",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "App",
                "note": "owns user",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Layout",
                "note": "passes only",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Header",
                "note": "passes only",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "UserMenu",
                "note": "actually reads it",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Composition Is the Cure",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// App owns user, builds the node",
            "<Layout",
            "  sidebar={<UserMenu user={user}/>}",
            "/>",
            "// Layout: {sidebar} — no user prop"
          ],
          "note": "JSX prop skips Layout entirely"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`children` and JSX props are created by the ==state owner==",
            "Middle components take opaque nodes, not data",
            "Zero levels of drilling, zero context needed"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useState(props.value)` — copy goes **stale** when prop changes",
            "Reaching for context at level two — premature; 3-4 levels is fine",
            "Lifting to the root by reflex when a mid parent shares both children"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Summary rule",
          "text": "Lift only as high as the __nearest shared owner__, never to the root. Then push everything else back down."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Context Is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Context is a ==broadcast channel== down the tree. It solves **distribution**, not storage — the value still lives in a `useState` or `useReducer` __above__ the provider.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const Ctx = createContext(null);",
            "<Ctx.Provider value={v}>",
            "  <Deep />",
            "</Ctx.Provider>",
            "const v = useContext(Ctx);"
          ],
          "note": "three pieces: create, provide, consume"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Propagation Rules",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Consumer re-renders when `value` changes by ==Object.is==",
            "Depth does not matter — 1 level or 20",
            "Context updates **bypass** `React.memo` in between",
            "Nested providers override outward-in; reads the __nearest__ one",
            "Default value used only when **no** Provider is above"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Silent bug",
          "text": "Forget the Provider and `useContext` quietly returns the default. No error — just a stale theme forever."
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Where state should live"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Context: Broadcast, Not Store",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Classic Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// new object EVERY render",
            "<Ctx.Provider",
            "  value={{user, setUser}}>",
            "// fix: stable identity",
            "const value = useMemo(",
            "  () => ({user, setUser}), [user]);"
          ],
          "note": "object literal = new ref = all consumers render"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Split the Contexts",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const [s, dispatch] =",
            "  useReducer(r, init);",
            "<StateCtx.Provider value={s}>",
            " <DispatchCtx.Provider",
            "   value={dispatch}>"
          ],
          "note": "dispatch is stable — that value never changes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Component reads",
            "Data change",
            "Action only"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "One merged ctx",
              "re-render",
              "re-render"
            ],
            [
              "StateContext",
              "re-render",
              "—"
            ],
            [
              "DispatchContext",
              "**no** render",
              "—"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Where It Fits",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{green:theme} light / dark toggle",
            "{green:locale} language, currency format",
            "{green:auth} session user object",
            "{green:flags} feature flags at boot"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Text input value with 30 consumers — per __keystroke__",
            "Mouse or animation-frame position — 60 renders/sec",
            "Anything needing ==selector subscriptions== (see page 9)"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Context = low-frequency, app-wide values. Memoize the value, split state from dispatch, and never broadcast a fast-changing one."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What a Re-render Costs",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A re-render is __not__ a repaint: React runs the function, ==diffs==, commits nothing if output is unchanged",
            "The cost is the **JS work** — calling components, allocating elements, walking the tree",
            "Default rule: a component re-renders, its ==entire subtree== re-renders",
            "Cheap subtrees re-render in {green:microseconds} — most are fine"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. React.memo",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const Row = React.memo(function Row(",
            "  {label, onPick}) {",
            "  return <li>{label}</li>",
            "})",
            "// skips render if props",
            "// shallow-equal (Object.is)"
          ],
          "note": "shallow compare, not deep"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "Distribution, not storage"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Re-render Cost and Memoization",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky-pink",
          "title": "memo defeated by",
          "text": "Any inline `{...}`, `[...]` or `() => {}` prop is a **new reference** every render, so shallow-equal always fails."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. useMemo vs useCallback",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const total = useMemo(",
            "  () => sum(items), [items])",
            "const onPick = useCallback(",
            "  id => sel(id), [sel])",
            "// useCallback(fn, deps) ===",
            "// useMemo(() => fn, deps)"
          ],
          "note": "one caches value, one caches fn"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Hook",
            "Caches",
            "Use for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`useMemo`",
              "a **value**",
              "expensive compute, object props"
            ],
            [
              "`useCallback`",
              "a **fn ref**",
              "handlers passed to `memo` kids"
            ],
            [
              "`React.memo`",
              "a **render**",
              "leaf under a chatty parent"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Memo Is Not Free",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every render still ==allocates== the closure and ==compares deps==",
            "Guarding a 3-node subtree costs more than re-rendering it",
            "Wrong order: measure with the **React DevTools Profiler** first"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Structural Fix Beats memo",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "// state down, not memo up",
            "<Chatty>",
            "  <Expensive />   {/* prop */}",
            "</Chatty>",
            "// children made by owner,",
            "// so not re-created"
          ],
          "note": "same element ref, no re-render"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Context Cannot Select",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`useContext` gives the ==whole value== — no subscribing to `state.cart.total`",
            "Any change to `value` wakes **every** consumer (see page 7)",
            "External stores select: subscribe to a slice, re-render on that slice only"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const total = useSyncExternalStore(",
            "  store.subscribe,",
            "  () => store.get().cart.total)"
          ],
          "note": "official hook for outside state"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "The real mistake",
          "text": "Memoizing everything by default: slower code, ==much harder to read==, and the deps arrays rot silently."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "react",
      "subtitle": "What re-renders cost"
    }
  ],
